{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Jira DC hardening — follow-on to e369\n\n## Context\n\nEpic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] delivered Jira Server/Data Center support and met its\noperator-approved exit bar (run **30964805133**: 62 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed). This epic holds\nthe DC work that delivery DISCOVERED, which is hardening not the feature.\nOperator decision 2026-08-05: let e369 close, harden here.\n\n## What is in scope — all three children CLOSED, all three changes MERGED to main\n\n* [rebar:4a6d-5bbc-44f4-4a56] (bug) — the capability-map channel **reports rather than fails**, so a\n  run made before any Software project exists silently writes a WRONG Epic-field contract. Its\n  ORIGINAL fix (a pre-run `await_required_fields` gate) was **REFUTED**; re-scoped to post-run\n  validation. **Change 1642 → `f487b62b3c`.**\n* [rebar:a3fa-e8d4-f4aa-4b51] (bug) — capability call sites are cast but not runtime-guarded, so a\n  non-capable transport fails silently. **Change 1634 → `671fa77c88`.**\n* [rebar:f020-0960-2c42-4d61] (task) — the dormant absence-probe port; ruled **DELETE**.\n  **Change 1645 → `b95c097fd4`.**\n\n## Explicitly NOT in scope\n\nCloud-surface defects from DC parity guards ([rebar:6194-...], [rebar:6a74-...], [rebar:9a46-...])\nare Cloud's. The vacuous-guard class ([rebar:8a5e-b88e-0c3e-4544]) and capability-map trust infra\n([rebar:a9bd-6641-e603-42bc]) have their own tickets.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] 4a6d is fixed per its recorded OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-12, option (a)): the capability-map\n      workflow validates the Epic-field contract AFTER the agent run and marks the report\n      UNVERIFIED / fails the job when the run cannot distinguish \"the image lacks the Epic fields\"\n      from \"no Software project existed yet\". A pre-run `await_required_fields` gate is OUT of\n      scope: bug 941b landed to REMOVE that call site and `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py` bans\n      it in terms; `main()` creates no project before the agent run, so the wait would deadlock. DELIVERED: `customfield_count()` in the shared readiness module — still the single\n      source of the field contract, now consulted AFTER the run — plus the pure\n      `epic_field_report_problem()` in `main()`'s finally block: `::error::` naming both 941b\n      candidate causes, exit 1, verdict in `run_metadata.json`, artifacts still written\n- [x] the map run FAILS rather than reports when the contract cannot be established — proven by a\n      test that pins a system-only inventory as not-ready on that surface, not merely by\n      config. DELIVERED: 12 cells in `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py` — system-only\n      inventory refused, provisioned accepted, no field read captured refused, a 401 read\n      not mistaken for an empty inventory, and two cells driving `main()` on both verdicts\n- [x] **AMENDED** — a3fa is fixed: the four capability call sites are RUNTIME-guarded and the two\n      states an operator must act on differently are reported DISTINCTLY through the EXISTING\n      bridge audit channel, not swallowed by the surrounding `except Exception`.\n      ABSENT is a designed skip (INFO log naming capability and site, plus a durable `bridge_alerts`\n      record under `outbound-<capability>-capability-absent`); PRESENT-BUT-RAISED keeps the existing\n      warning and `comment_errors` capture with the exception surfaced.\n      *This replaces \"…fails loudly rather than silently, with a test that pins the loud failure\",\n      which prescribed the WRONG outcome:* the operator ruling on a3fa (2026-08-12) is\n      skip-vs-failure reported DISTINCTLY, not a hard failure on absence — an unimplemented OPT-IN\n      capability on a second backend is by design no error. Pinned by a mutation-checked test:\n      deleting the guard operand turns `test_dispatch_links_absent_capability_is_a_designed_skip`\n      RED on the ALERT-KIND assertion, not on an incidental `AttributeError`\n- [x] **AMENDED (guard shape)** — the guard is `isinstance` PRIMARY with a `hasattr(client, member)`\n      fallback, a deliberate in-code-documented divergence from the isinstance-only shape a3fa's\n      plan text and ADR-0083 §193-198 specify. Since Python 3.12 (gh-102433) a `@runtime_checkable`\n      `isinstance` resolves members via `inspect.getattr_static`, so a transport forwarding through\n      `__getattr__` is declared capability-absent and its writes skipped BY DESIGN — reinstating\n      this very defect, blessed as intentional. CI runs 3.11 AND 3.12, so a version bump is no\n      alternative. Pinned by `test_proxying_transport_is_capable_and_is_not_skipped` behind a\n      `sys.version_info` split; ADR divergence in [rebar:5c21-f24a-f7f8-4a55]\n- [x] [operator-attested] f020 is decided AND EXECUTED, the decision recorded with its reason,\n      including what it does to e369 AC5's both-backends claim on `classify_probe_response`. The\n      decision record lives on tickets f020 and e369, outside the repo snapshot, hence the tag; the\n      EXECUTION is in-repo. The operator ruled DELETE; change 1645 (`b95c097fd4`)\n      removed `SupportsAbsenceProbe`, all three `probe_remote` impls, `inbound_probe.py`,\n      `adapters/jira/probe.py` and `adapters/jira_family/probe.py` (28 files, +73/-1033) after\n      proving zero live callers by BOTH a semantic search and a string grep.\n      Effect on e369: `classify_probe_response` is REMOVED from AC5's shared-unit list and **e369's\n      AC5 is amended on that ticket to say so**, narrowing the \"one shared implementation imported\n      by both backends\" claim to the field/value maps, the label sanitizer and the link-relation\n      vocabulary — a scope reduction, not a regression: no unit was forked per adapter. The orphaned\n      `jira.resolved_statuses` / `reconciler.resolved_statuses` keys are a user-visible surface\n      change, deferred to [rebar:549c-032f-6cb0-4258] behind the config-read gate's `# read-via:`\n      marker, which expires when it closes\n- [x] [operator-attested] **AMENDED** — this epic's changes did not regress the live DC harness; the\n      run evidence lives in GitHub Actions, outside the repo snapshot. *The original wording, \"the\n      live DC harness is still GREEN end to end after this epic's changes (0 failed cells)\",\n      inherited from e369's exit bar, is not certifiable as written: the harness was ALREADY red\n      before any of this epic's changes landed, for a cause that is not this epic's.* Scheduled run\n      **31362329118** (2026-08-10, head `351e13bbda` — BEFORE changes 1642/1634/1645 landed) ended\n      **3 failed, 59 passed, 1 xfailed** with the container up cleanly — not a readiness or infra\n      abort. Two failures are stale assertions on an `OK:` line commit `c87afedba8` stopped emitting\n      on the canonical `sync` route while the pass in fact converged; the third is a runner git-lock\n      timeout. Filed as [rebar:9590-34f5-21a8-41fc], linked `discovered_from` this epic, which\n      carries the 0-failed re-green bar forward. What IS established here: none of the three changes\n      touches any cell in that failure set, and each landed `Verified +1` (full CI) plus, for the\n      reconciler change, the mutation check above\n- [x] [operator-attested] no cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green (the standing\n      operator constraint); the harness run's cell inventory lives in GitHub Actions, outside the\n      repo snapshot. Held: no live-DC harness cell was deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed by any of the\n      three changes, and the run's single `xfail` (`test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips`) is\n      pre-existing, owned by 2b16. The three probe-only unit modules deleted by change 1645 are NOT\n      an instance of this: they existed solely to exercise the units the operator ruled deleted and\n      went with their subject in a pure deletion — no assertion weakened, no failing cell removed\n## Testing\n\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 -q; make lint typecheck"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786527996765110001,"uuid":"ad199ee7-5029-4951-9adf-6aa050233f4b"}